#!/bin/sh
# The fork of Idris's compiler (compiler/idris) carries the change of
# upstream/21-termination-closure/pull-request.diff: a termination check
# closes the size-change graphs over the calls inside strongly connected
# components only, and records as terminating every function a successful
# search settles. Main.idr's 25 total functions each reach a chain of 240
# covering functions with no loop; the fork checks them in about a second
# (arm64 macOS), and the pinned, unpatched checker takes minutes, past the
# step limit. When a re-sync brings upstream's fix, the report, its PINS.md
# entry and this test go (upstream/README.md).
. "$IDRIS_MLIR_ROOT/tests/testutils.sh"
profile_accept .
